# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Development happens on Windows, which checks out CRLF by default and produced
# whole-file CRLF churn in diffs. `text=auto` stores LF in git and leaves the
# working copy alone, so diffs show real changes only.
#
# NOTE: this applies to files as they are next touched. A one-time
# `git add --renormalize .` would convert everything at once, but that rewrites
# every file in a single commit — do it deliberately as its own change, never
# alongside feature work.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never convert.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
